## ANNEX G

( Clause 6.2.2 )

INFORMATION TO BE SUBMITTED FOR TYPE APPROVAL OF TYRES

1.  Manufacturer’s name and address;
2.  Telephone No.;
3.  Fax. No.;
4.  E-mail address;
5.  Contact person;
6.  Tyre-size designation;
7.  Trade-name or mark;
8.  Category of use (normal/special/snow);
9.  Structure: diagonal (bias ply/bias belted)/ radial;
10.  Speed category;
10.1 Nominal;
10.2 Additional (if applicable);
11.  Ply Rating and maximum load in kg (corresponding to ply rating) and/or load index and maximum load in kg (corresponding to nominal speed and load index) and additional load index (corresponding to additional speed) as applicable;
12.  Whether the tyre is to be used with or without an inner tube;
13.  Whether the tyre is normal or reinforced;
14.  Overall width (mm);
15.  Overall diameter (mm);
16.  Rim on which tyre can be mounted;


17.  Measuring rim and test rim;
18.  Inflation pressure for dimensional measurements (kPa);
18.1 Cold Inflation Pressure, in kPa corresponding to maximum load carrying capacity;
18.2  Test inflation pressure, kPa;
19.  Factor X referred to in 3.30 in case of theoretical (imaginary) rim, if applicable;
20.  Intended for use on (type of vehicle);
21. If tyre size is not listed in Tables 6 to 28 and/or tyre sizes with a different ply rating and/or load-inflation details other than those given in Table 6 to 28, reference to Standards Manuals of organizations like The European Tyre and Rim Technical Organisation (ETRTO), Indian Tyre Technical Advisory Committee (ITTAC), The Japan Automobile Tyre Manufacturers’ Association (JATMA), The Tire and Rim Association, Inc. (T & RA-US);
22.  Numbers and height of tread wear indicator;
23.  Type of tread pattern (Lug, Rib, Semi-lug or Block); and
24.  Drawing or photograph in triplicate identifying tyre tread pattern side wall marking and relevant dimensions of inflated tyre mounted on the measuring rim.
